{"base_rate":0.40298507462686567,"brier":0.17625169606512886,"bss":0.26741308922558926,"bss_hi":0.36006843805000777,"bss_lo":0.1747134979917513,"chart":{"base":[410.4,172.4],"fp":[326.8,166.1],"lead":"62,283 272,256.4 482,205 692,129.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 41% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +23pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 94% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 9%; promised 96% → rained 74%"},"rel":"78.3,426.2 354.1,317.1 664.8,146.4"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1374084124830394,"ess":343.16737537376235,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for &#x27;s-Hertogenbosch</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The &#x27;s-Hertogenbosch rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNULAND, 8.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 128 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(72&ndash;159) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>219</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>223</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>&#x27;s-Hertogenbosch</b> <span class=\"muted\">Netherlands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;40% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 40% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>72&ndash;159\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    &#x27;s-Hertogenbosch &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for &#x27;s-Hertogenbosch\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.21232876712329,377.013698630137 90.57756756756757,322.97297297297297 166.75666666666666,230.33333333333331 274.6386842105263,123.36842105263156 359.4819178082192,42.9315068493151 408.872735426009,18.0 408.872735426009,26.161434977578438 359.4819178082192,102.76712328767127 274.6386842105263,195.21052631578945 166.75666666666666,306.16666666666663 90.57756756756757,372.1621621621622 59.21232876712329,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"235.3134328358209\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"235.3134328358209\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.21232876712329,358.73059360730593 90.57756756756757,318.05405405405406 166.75666666666666,291.0 274.6386842105263,223.94736842105263 359.4819178082192,177.56164383561642 408.872735426009,91.45291479820628\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 219 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.21232876712329\" cy=\"358.73059360730593\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"90.57756756756757\" cy=\"318.05405405405406\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"166.75666666666666\" cy=\"291.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"274.6386842105263\" cy=\"223.94736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"359.4819178082192\" cy=\"177.56164383561642\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 223 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.872735426009\" cy=\"91.45291479820628\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In &#x27;s-Hertogenbosch the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.16).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.162</td><td class='num'>14.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.186</td><td class='num'>16.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.236</td><td class='num'>14.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.375</td><td class='num'>12.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.69917,"lon":5.30417,"n":737,"n_cities":216,"name":"'s-Hertogenbosch","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003424657534246575,"n":219,"obs":0.0639269406392694,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09202702702702703,"n":74,"obs":0.17567567567567569,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.30722222222222223,"n":72,"obs":0.25,"sig":false},{"hi":0.76,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.6119736842105263,"n":76,"obs":0.4342105263157895,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.76,"mean":0.8516438356164384,"n":73,"obs":0.5616438356164384,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9911659192825113,"n":223,"obs":0.7982062780269058,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.0,"provisional":false,"rank":128,"rank_hi":159.02499999999998,"rank_lo":71.975,"reliability":0.0249648976502291,"resolution":0.09149152768797654,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"s-hertogenbosch","station":"NULAND","timezone":"Europe/Amsterdam"}